{"name":"Freshwater","hex":"#4da6b2","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Freshwater","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A place name:\nA large village and civil parish in the west of the Isle of Wight, England . \nA settlement on Bell Island, Newfoundland and Labrador, Canada.\nA designated place at Conception Bay, Newfoundland and Labrador.\nA neighbourhood of Placentia, Newfoundland and Labrador.\nAn unincorporated community in Humboldt County, California, United States.\nAn unincorporated community in Nelson County, Virginia, United States.\nA northern suburb of Sydney in Northern Beaches council area, New South Wales, Australia.\nA suburb of Cairns in Cairns Region, Queensland, Australia.","A large village and civil parish in the west of the Isle of Wight, England ."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Freshwater"}],"entries":[{"title":"Fresh water","blocks":[{"text":"Fresh water or freshwater is any naturally occurring liquid or frozen water containing low concentrations of dissolved salts and other total dissolved solids. The term excludes seawater and brackish water, but it does include non-salty mineral-rich waters, such as chalybeate springs. Fresh water may encompass frozen and meltwater in ice sheets, ice caps, glaciers, snowfields and icebergs, natural precipitations such as rainfall, snowfall, hail/sleet and graupel, and surface runoffs that form inland bodies of water such as wetlands, ponds, lakes, rivers, streams, as well as groundwater contained in aquifers, subterranean rivers and lakes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Amazonas%2C_Iquitos_-_Leticia%2C_Kolumbien_%2811472506936%29.jpg/330px-Amazonas%2C_Iquitos_-_Leticia%2C_Kolumbien_%2811472506936%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fresh_water","wikidata":"Q102192"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thu